[{:db/id 17592186347121 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/b6d469b24061f0f7284691b2e2f26a2c28d9557ab72a1c8ba3cad93eb65dde91.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}2{z}^{2}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/9190139502ef900218e3c3b186295627af2a1370b9f7d789366dac6474251b54.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{x}{3}-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/aa02840c9fa15e5e5048608fff81ad9f0a5623821a57366bf12ec6d60332bc9e.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{x}{3}-z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x/3-z}2{z}^{2}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x/3-z}2{z}^{2}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3-x/3-z}2{z}^{2}\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{z}^{2}[y]_{y=0}^{y=3-x/3-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{z}^{2}(3-\\frac{x}{3}-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(6{z}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}x{z}^{2}-2{z}^{3})\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(6{z}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}x{z}^{2}-2{z}^{3})\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(6{z}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}x{z}^{2}-2{z}^{3})\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[2{z}^{3}-\\frac{2}{9}x{z}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(8-\\frac{16}{9}x)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(8-\\frac{16}{9}x)\\,dx & ={[8x-\\frac{16}{18}{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =(24-8)-0 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
